Local fix to NVIDIA Streamline v2.14.16 include/sl_pcl.h (thirdparty/streamline/include).

Under C++23 (__cplusplus == 202302L) the header declares

    using to_underlying = std::to_underlying;

which is ill-formed (a type alias cannot name a function template), so every C++23 translation
unit that includes sl_pcl.h (and sl_reflex.h, which includes it) fails to compile with clang:
"no type named 'to_underlying' in namespace 'std'". The fix makes the header always take its own
fallback template:

--- a/include/sl_pcl.h
+++ b/include/sl_pcl.h
@@
 // c++23 has to_underlying implementation
-#if __cplusplus == 202302L
+// Local fix (pgr4 project): "using to_underlying = std::to_underlying;" below is ill-formed (an
+// alias of a function template) and breaks every C++23 build; always use the fallback.
+#if 0 && __cplusplus == 202302L
 using to_underlying = std::to_underlying;
 #else

(The edit also normalized the file's line endings from CRLF to LF.)
